          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %strong direct sum
            = succeed "," do
              %strong weak direct product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            that actually makes sense in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphisms"} zero morphisms
            (that is, any category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} co
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            exist.
          %p
            A basic and familiar example is the direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \oplus V_2
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2
            over some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            a set and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i\}_{i \in I}
            an
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigoplus_{i \in I} V_i
            is the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
            of elements in each of the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
            = succeed "," do
              %em an element in a direct sum is a sum of elements
          %p
            This generalises in two distinct ways, which we call
            %em direct sums
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em weak direct products
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            but the infinitary versions are (almost always) different.
          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            The name ‘weak direct product’ comes from the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            that is created by the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            of the direct product (and the entire direct product in finitary cases). But here we will not restrict ourselves to the context of such a concrete category.
          %p
            The term ‘direct sum’ comes from the finitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
            (simultaneously product and coproduct) in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive categories
          %p
            In the classical examples of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphisms"} zero morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i)_{i \in I}
            be an
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family"} family
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A : I \to Obj(\mathcal{C})
          %p
            We now define both the direct sum and weak direct product of this family. The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
            will be called the
            %strong direct summands
            or (weak)
            = succeed "." do
              %strong direct factors
          %h3#direct_sum Direct sum
          %p
            Here we must assume moreover that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            (or otherwise has a good concept of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              be the morphism from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_i A_i
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_i A_i
              characterized by having the following components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Id
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi A
                                    %mi i
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mn 0
                                %mi ij
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi i
                              %mo ≠
                              %mi j
                              %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    A_i \to \coprod A \stackrel{r}{\to} \prod A \to A_j
                    \\right)
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    Id_{A_i} &amp; if\; i = j
                    \\\
                    0_{ij} &amp; if\; i \neq j
                    ,}
                    \\right.
                    \\,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 0
                      %mi ij
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0_{ij}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j
            %p
              The
              %strong direct sum
              over the family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_i\}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} coim
                        %mi r
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} im
                        %mi r
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_i A_i \overset{\coim r}\to \bigoplus_i A_i \overset{\im r}\to \prod_i A_i
            %p
              of the morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              requires that the index set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              have
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              over the category of sets and
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+functions"} partial functions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the category of pointed sets, and the embedding is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              if and only if the law of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              holds. But the usual examples of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              are not (constructively) so enriched. Fortunately, the usual examples of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              have decidable equality.
          %h3#weak_direct_product Weak direct product
          %p
            Here we consider the finitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in F} A_i
          %p
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            varies over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite subsets
            of the index set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuratowski+finite"} Kuratowski finite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is actually finite in the strictest sense.)
          %p
            These finite products form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+limit"} direct system
            indexed by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction"} directed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mi fin
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}_{fin}I
            of finite subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            (ordered by inclusion) with the map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in F} A_i \to \prod_{i \in G} A_i ,
          %p
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≅
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi F
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≅
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in F} A_i \cong \prod_{i \in F} A_i \times \prod_{i \in G \setminus F} 1 \stackrel{(id, 0)}{\to} \prod_{i \in F} A_i \times \prod_{i \in G \setminus F} A_i \cong \prod_{i \in G} A_i .
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If it exists, the
              %strong weak direct product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                      %mi wk
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod^wk_i A_i
              is defined to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+limit"} directed colimit
              of this direct system.
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              In the categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"}> abelian
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              in both categories.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+product"} free product
            %p
              So in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
